---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects & Work Planning — Task Tracking, Timesheets, Project Costing"
  description="Project register, task management, resource allocation, milestone tracking, timesheets, project costing, and billing. Part of Kraal Code ERP."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/capabilities/projects/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/en/capabilities/">Capabilities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Projects & Work Planning</li></ol></nav>
      <h1>Projects & Work Planning</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">Track projects from initiation to closure. Allocate resources, record time, manage budgets, and generate project profitability reports.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>Project managers, team leads, consultants, and business owners who deliver work on a project basis. Whether you run construction projects, consulting engagements, donor-funded programmes, or internal initiatives, this module keeps projects on time and on budget.</p>
    <p>If your organisation bills by the hour, tracks milestones for donors, manages multiple concurrent projects, or needs to know which projects are profitable and which are leaking money — this module gives you that visibility without a separate project management tool.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Project Register</h3><p>Create projects with start/end dates, budgets, responsible managers, and client references. Track project status from initiation through planning, execution, and closure.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Task Management</h3><p>Break projects into tasks and subtasks. Assign responsibilities. Set due dates and dependencies. Track completion status. Generate task-level progress reports.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Resource Allocation</h3><p>Assign team members to projects and tasks. Track allocation percentages. Identify over-allocated resources. Balance workload across the team.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Timesheets</h3><p>Record time spent on projects and tasks. Approve timesheets through workflow. Use timesheet data for project costing and client billing.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Project Budgeting</h3><p>Set project budgets by category (labour, materials, expenses). Track budget vs actual with variance analysis. Alert when spending approaches budget limits.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Project Billing</h3><p>Generate client invoices from timesheets and project milestones. Support fixed-price and time-and-materials billing models. Track billed vs unbilled amounts.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Milestone Tracking</h3><p>Define project milestones with target dates and deliverables. Track milestone completion. Generate milestone status reports for clients and donors. Link milestones to billing triggers.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Project Profitability</h3><p>Compare project revenue against total cost (labour, materials, expenses). Calculate profit margin per project. Identify loss-making projects early. Generate profitability reports by client, type, or manager.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>How it connects</h2>
    <p>Projects draw resources from HR, materials from procurement, and post costs to accounting. Every entry flows through the ledger:</p>
    <ul class="connection-list">
      <li><strong>HR</strong> → resource availability from leave and attendance data, labour rates for costing</li>
      <li><strong>Accounting</strong> → project costs accumulated in GL, project revenue recognised on billing</li>
      <li><strong>Sales</strong> → project invoices generated through the sales module</li>
      <li><strong>Procurement</strong> → project-specific purchases tracked against project budgets</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Controls and permissions</h2>
    <div class="controls-grid">
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Budget Authority</h3><p>Project budgets require project manager and finance approval. Budget overruns trigger alerts. Exceeding budget by more than 10% requires director sign-off.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Timesheet Approval</h3><p>Timesheets require supervisor approval before they count toward project costing. Unapproved time is excluded from billing and cost calculations. Weekly submission deadlines enforced.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Billing Review</h3><p>Project invoices generated from timesheets require project manager review before issuance. Prevents overbilling and ensures work was delivered before invoicing.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Audit Trail</h3><p>Every project creation, task assignment, timesheet entry, budget change, and billing event is logged with user, timestamp, and IP. INSERT-only log. No project record can be silently altered.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>See it in action</h2>
    <p class="screenshot-intro">Screenshots from the live Kraal Code system — coming soon.</p>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Project Register</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Task Board</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Timesheet Entry</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Project Profitability</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section--dark section"><div class="container text-center">
    <h2>See projects in action</h2>
    <p>Request a demonstration tailored to your project management needs.</p>
    <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-4xl);
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  .page-hero-subtext {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .breadcrumb ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--kc-teal);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '/';
    margin-left: var(--kc-space-2);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .container--narrow {
    max-width: var(--kc-container-narrow);
  }
  .container--narrow p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--kc-leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-8);
  }
  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-6);
    background: var(--kc-surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }
  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .feature-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list {
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .connection-list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list strong {
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .controls-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .control-item {
    padding: var(--kc-space-5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--kc-teal);
  }
  .control-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-1);
  }
  .control-item p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .screenshot-intro {
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background: var(--kc-surface-warm);
    border: 2px dashed var(--kc-border);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .screenshot-label {
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .screenshot-note {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .btn--inverse {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
    border: 2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);
    transition: all var(--kc-transition-fast);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .btn--inverse:hover {
    background: var(--kc-teal);
    border-color: var(--kc-teal);
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-hero h1 {
      font-size: var(--kc-text-3xl);
    }
    .feature-grid,
    .controls-grid,
    .screenshot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
